Independent Review &#8226; Sponsored Content</p>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <h1 class="vy-adv-content__heading vy-weight-normal" style="margin-bottom: var(--heading-margin-heading_6ea9tG); text-align:left;">
              Can You Really Detox Your Lungs? Here Is What to Know Before You Buy Another Cleanse, Tea or Detox Kit
            </h1>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__body-content vy-content-default vy-body-content-content_YbcBng" style="margin-bottom: var(--content-margin-content_YbcBng); text-align:left;"><p>Updated: September 2026 &#183; 8 min read</p></div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__divider" style="margin-bottom: var(--divider-margin-divider_EbrGpz); background: #cccccc"></div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__image-content vy-size-large vy-has-mob-image_7WFgVn " style="margin-bottom: var(--image-margin-image_7WFgVn)">
              
                
                <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-1.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                  
                    object-position: top">
                
                  <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-1.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                    
                      object-position: top">
                
                
              
            </div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__body-content vy-content-default vy-body-content-content_GNGbiG" style="margin-bottom: var(--content-margin-content_GNGbiG); text-align:left;"><p>I typed lung detox into a search bar at about two in the morning, which is how most of these things start. What came back was teas, patches, three day cleanses and salt inhalers, every one of them promising to flush years of build up out of me by the weekend.</p><p>Then I noticed something <strong>none of them mentioned</strong> anywhere on the page. Not one explained what the lungs already do on their own. They all started from the same assumption, that my lungs were a clogged drain and the right purchase would rinse them out.</p><p>It took a few weeks of reading before it landed: <strong>your lungs are not a filter you can rinse out</strong>.</p><p>Nearly everything sold as a cleanse <em>skips past how the organ works</em>. Some of it is harmless. Some of it is expensive water. Either way it is aimed at a problem that does not work the way the label suggests.</p><p><strong>So what is actually worth doing?&nbsp;</strong></p><p>Less than the detox industry would like you to think, and it costs less too. I ended up on a daily liquid with two ingredients in it, mullein and chlorophyll, at $34.95 a bottle. No protocol, no flush, no week booked off.</p><p><strong>Here are 5 things </strong>worth understanding before you spend money on a lung cleanse, starting with the one that<strong> </strong>took me longest to accept.</p></div>
          
      
        
