            <style>/**/</style>
            <h2 class="vy-adv-content__heading vy-weight-normal" style="margin-bottom: var(--heading-margin-heading_w4GrKb); text-align:left;">
              Detox Teas and Cleanse Kits Cannot Reach Your Lungs.
            </h2>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__image-content vy-size-large vy-has-mob-image_MGFgK8 " style="margin-bottom: var(--image-margin-image_MGFgK8)">
              
                
                <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-3.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                  
                    object-position: top">
                
                  <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-3.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                    
                      object-position: top">
                
                
              
            </div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__body-content vy-content-default vy-body-content-content_FMp6rW" style="margin-bottom: var(--content-margin-content_FMp6rW); text-align:left;"><p><strong>Then there are the detox teas.</strong></p><p>Some of them are pleasant enough. I am not going to pretend otherwise. But have you ever read what a lung detox tea is actually claiming?</p><p>Read the label properly.</p><p>It goes down into your stomach. That is the digestive tract, and it is a completely separate route from your airways. Whatever is in the cup never reaches lung tissue at all. The word lung is doing all the work on the front of the box and nothing behind it.</p><p>That is not a lung product. <strong>That is a herbal tea with better marketing.</strong></p><p>The rest of the aisle is much the same. Patches that sit on the skin. Salt lamps that colour a room nicely. Cleanse kits sold in seven day blocks, priced so the next block is due before you have decided whether the first one did anything at all.</p><p>What I settled on is deliberately duller than any of that. BetterLungs is a liquid you add to water once a day. Mullein and chlorophyll, made in the US, formulated by a pharmacist. It does not claim to flush anything, and that is a large part of why I trusted it over the kits.</p><p>It costs $34.95 a bottle, and one bottle is a 30 day supply. <strong>No protocol to follow, no week set aside, nothing to recover from.</strong></p></div>
          
      
    </div>
  </div>
</div>


<style>/**/</style></div><div id="shopify-section-template--27892684030136__adv_main_content_TcC8tM" class="vy-shopify-section">

<link data-vy-stripped="">
<link data-vy-stripped="">



<style>/**/</style>

<div id="adv-content-template--27892684030136__adv_main_content_TcC8tM" class="vy-adv-content">
  <div class="vy-adv-content__wrapper">
