            <style>/**/</style>
            <h2 class="vy-adv-content__heading vy-weight-normal" style="margin-bottom: var(--heading-margin-heading_geMpaD); text-align:left;">
              Mullein Has Been a Lung Herb for Centuries.
            </h2>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__image-content vy-size-large " style="margin-bottom: var(--image-margin-image_Rt9KDa)">
              
                
                <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-6.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                  
                    object-position: top">
                
                
              
            </div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__body-content vy-content-default vy-body-content-content_p3TaJy" style="margin-bottom: var(--content-margin-content_p3TaJy); text-align:left;"><p><strong>This is the part I did not expect to find interesting.</strong></p><p>Mullein is a tall weed with soft, felted leaves that grows on roadsides and waste ground across Europe and North America. Most people walk straight past it. It has been used for lung support for a very long time, long enough that the written record reaches back to Greek and Roman medicine.</p><p>I had assumed it was a modern wellness invention.</p><p>It is not. The tradition is a great deal older than the marketing. <strong>That history is why it is here.</strong></p><p>Betterbrand builds BetterLungs on a mullein leaf extract, and the reason it leads the formula is that long record of traditional use for respiratory support rather than a claim written for a label. Traditional use is not the same thing as proof, and I would rather say so plainly than dress it up.</p><p>What I like about it is how unexciting the pitch is. A plant people have leaned on for lung support for centuries, in a liquid you take daily. No flush, no reset, no countdown running in the corner.</p><p>The second ingredient is chlorophyll, which is the next thing worth knowing about, and the reason the liquid is dark green rather than brown.</p><p>Between them they are the whole formula. Two actives and nothing else doing the work, which is rarer on a supplement shelf than it ought to be.</p></div>
          
      
