            <style>/**/</style>
            <h2 class="vy-adv-content__heading vy-weight-normal" style="margin-bottom: var(--heading-margin-heading_tGVTPT); text-align:left;">
              Chlorophyll, Oxygen Flow and Steady Everyday Energy.
            </h2>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__image-content vy-size-large " style="margin-bottom: var(--image-margin-image_yfdK98)">
              
                
                <img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/vysta/lp-762-betterbrand/images/img-7.jpg" width="100%" height="auto" style="
                  
                    object-position: top">
                
                
              
            </div>
          
      
        
            <style>/**/</style>
            <div class="vy-adv-content__body-content vy-content-default vy-body-content-content_XCVH6X" style="margin-bottom: var(--content-margin-content_XCVH6X); text-align:left;"><p><strong>This is the one that decided it for me.</strong></p><p>Chlorophyll is the pigment that makes plants green, the molecule doing the work in photosynthesis. In a supplement it is there for its antioxidant properties and for its part in supporting healthy oxygen flow in the body.</p><p>You will see it sold on its own as a green drink, usually in a sachet with a lot of packaging around it. Here it is simply the second half of the formula, already in the liquid, which is one fewer thing to buy and one fewer thing to remember.</p><p>Supporting healthy oxygen flow and steady everyday energy is the kind of claim I can live with, because it describes what an ingredient does rather than promising me an outcome.</p><p>It is also why the bottle is meant to be taken daily rather than in a burst. Antioxidant support and healthy oxygen flow are ongoing, everyday functions. They are not something you top up once a quarter and forget about.</p><p>Set against a detox kit, it is an almost boring proposition. Two plant ingredients that support respiratory health and healthy oxygen flow, taken once a day, for a bit over a dollar a day.</p><p>Mullein and chlorophyll. <strong>One liquid covers both</strong>, which is the part I keep repeating to people, because I had been pricing them up separately before I found this.</p></div>
          
      
        
